Planning a trip with more than one stop? Most flight sites search one leg at a time.

RouteHound lets you add the whole trip: every city and date. It compares flights, trains, ferries and stays, then gives you a few smart picks with the reason for each.

Free to use. {link}

Flexible by a day or two? RouteHound shows each leg's fares by day, so you can spot a cheaper date before you book.

Try it with our example trip: {link}

(Some links are affiliate links; it doesn't change your price.)

Hi all, I made a free tool for multi-city trips and the rules allow sharing tools, so here it is.

You add every leg of the trip once, and RouteHound compares flights, trains, ferries and stays, with a short reason for each pick. It also shows fares by day for each leg.

Disclosure: I built it and some booking links are affiliate links (no change to your price). Honest feedback very welcome: {link}
